1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,070
Characters, actions, places, occupations,
and events in this series

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,750
are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.

3
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:13,280
They are not intended to urge
or promote any behavior in the series.

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,720
Viewer discretion is advised.

5
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:18,500
Chan.

6
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:22,160
You are Chan’s ex?

7
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:26,240
I’m so sorry for putting you through this.

8
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:27,730
I love you.

9
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:31,260
Even though
you still don’t love me, it’s okay.

10
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:33,720
But I will always love you.

11
00:00:36,210 --> 00:00:37,050
Mom.

12
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:40,700
Mom.

13
00:02:00,630 --> 00:02:01,450
Key.

14
00:02:02,110 --> 00:02:03,070
What’s wrong?

15
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:04,780
Did you have a nightmare?

16
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:08,729
It’s okay.

17
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:10,360
Look at me.

18
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,500
Look into my eyes.

19
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,900
It’s okay. It’s just a bad dream.

20
00:02:28,030 --> 00:02:29,700
Was the dream that scary?

21
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:32,800
Chan.

22
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:41,570
Why are you crying?

23
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:44,800
It’s just a bad dream.

24
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,500
Try to go back to sleep.

25
00:04:20,610 --> 00:04:21,800
Here is your breakfast.

26
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:27,700
It will get tastier

27
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:30,700
if you get a kiss from me.

28
00:04:56,170 --> 00:04:57,100
What?

29
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:01,700
Do you want another kiss?

30
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,730
Can you stop pretending
as if nothing happened?

31
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,800
Pretending?

32
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:24,100
About last night.

33
00:05:25,070 --> 00:05:26,300
You had a nightmare.

34
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:30,600
It’s nothing.

35
00:05:31,510 --> 00:05:32,900
It’s just a bad dream.

36
00:05:36,330 --> 00:05:38,380
Everyone has a bad dream
from time to time.

37
00:05:39,730 --> 00:05:41,300
Have you never had one?

38
00:05:45,409 --> 00:05:47,700
Why are you this stubborn?

39
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:51,000
Chan, my cheek is all stretched out.

40
00:05:51,659 --> 00:05:53,010
Can’t you give me a kiss instead?

41
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:56,900
You are so stubborn.

42
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:02,400
Fine.

43
00:06:03,210 --> 00:06:04,300
I’ll tell you.

44
00:06:06,810 --> 00:06:08,230
Last night,

45
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:11,100
I dreamt that you dumped me.

46
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:14,240
So I got scared.

47
00:06:16,850 --> 00:06:19,600
Do you see how much I love you?

48
00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:27,200
Are you sure that was the dream?

49
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:30,200
Yes.

50
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,380
Right, Simba?

51
00:06:41,050 --> 00:06:43,159
It’s time for breakfast.

52
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,850
Come here and have breakfast with Mama.

53
00:06:54,159 --> 00:06:55,400
Let’s eat breakfast.

54
00:06:55,970 --> 00:06:59,900
Let’s have breakfast with Mama.

55
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:01,650
Come on.

56
00:07:10,410 --> 00:07:11,400
Dig in.

57
00:07:21,170 --> 00:07:22,400
Enjoy your meal.

58
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:35,960
Arrange her hair on the left.

59
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:41,500
Thank you.

60
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:45,900
Lift your chin a little.

61
00:07:50,850 --> 00:07:52,250
Please arrange her dress.

62
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:56,900
Sun, lift your chin.

63
00:07:57,670 --> 00:07:59,200
Sun, look at the mirror.

64
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,050
Look deep into the mirror.

65
00:08:07,910 --> 00:08:09,400
Let’s take a break for 15 minutes.

66
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:17,300
I’m sorry, Peach.

67
00:08:17,570 --> 00:08:20,250
I can’t really concentrate today.

68
00:08:21,190 --> 00:08:22,200
It’s okay.

69
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,500
We all have days when we feel tired.

70
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:26,650
Please take a break. You will feel better.

71
00:08:26,970 --> 00:08:28,050
I’m sorry.

72
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:29,800
Thank you.

73
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:32,700
Key.

74
00:08:36,650 --> 00:08:38,210
What are you doing here?

75
00:08:39,210 --> 00:08:41,549
When I heard that
you have a photoshoot with Sun today,

76
00:08:41,590 --> 00:08:43,049
I rushed to see you.

77
00:08:44,030 --> 00:08:46,500
You two know each other?

78
00:08:47,870 --> 00:08:49,900
This is Key, my sister.

79
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:55,930
You’re not rushing off anywhere, are you?

80
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:57,500
Let’s go eat together after this.

81
00:08:58,310 --> 00:08:59,200
Okay.

82
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:07,200
It’s really a small world, isn’t it?

83
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:09,580
Yes.

84
00:09:11,570 --> 00:09:13,100
Since you are here,

85
00:09:13,370 --> 00:09:15,800
can we talk?

86
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:18,880
Talk about what?

87
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:23,400
Something is bothering me.

88
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,240
Is it…

89
00:09:30,110 --> 00:09:31,640
about Jay?

90
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:38,530
I will be abroad for one month.

91
00:09:38,910 --> 00:09:42,290
I want you to take care of
my sister for me.

92
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,100
I already met her.

93
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,720
She suddenly came into Chan’s room.

94
00:09:48,050 --> 00:09:51,400
Jay still has the keycard to Chan’s room?

95
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:54,400
This is not good.

96
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:56,700
I’ll tell Chan to change the keycard.

97
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:59,800
Otherwise, she will never
leave Chan alone.

98
00:10:00,070 --> 00:10:03,100
I don’t think Chan will soften up easily
and take her back.

99
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:07,330
She seems so guarded, almost cold.

100
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:10,600
We never know, Key.

101
00:10:10,970 --> 00:10:14,130
Chan is guarded and resolute.

102
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:18,300
But when it comes to Jay,
she always gives in to her.

103
00:10:19,860 --> 00:10:22,900
That brat is always an exception for Chan.

104
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:32,160
Is it that serious?

105
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:33,500
Yes.

106
00:10:34,590 --> 00:10:37,900
She is the type
who always gets what she wants,

107
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:40,300
no matter what it takes.

108
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:44,300
She is scary.

109
00:10:48,380 --> 00:10:50,700
I don’t want to see my sister hurt again.

110
00:11:03,450 --> 00:11:05,100
Sun, can you tell me?

111
00:11:06,590 --> 00:11:09,580
What kind of person is Jay?

112
00:11:22,810 --> 00:11:23,900
Miss Chan.

113
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:27,730
I prepared the details of the banquet
at the ballroom for you.

114
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:32,000
Can you check Mr. Kim’s proposal for me?

115
00:11:32,390 --> 00:11:33,300
Sure, Miss Chan.

116
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:47,920
FOR MY MOON.
—YOUR J.

117
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:09,070
So you still remember
what my favorite flower is.

118
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:38,930
ARE YOU FREE TONIGHT?
DO YOU WANT TO WATCH ME SING?

119
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:52,530
I’LL THINK ABOUT IT.

120
00:12:56,160 --> 00:13:01,250
IF I’M FREE, I’LL GO.

121
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,800
Let’s do our best like always.

122
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:17,060
Okay.

123
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:18,600
Hold the tempo for me.

124
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:39,500
Hello, Miss Chan.

125
00:13:46,910 --> 00:13:48,200
You really came to see me.

126
00:13:48,950 --> 00:13:50,300
You are so sweet.

127
00:13:51,790 --> 00:13:54,900
I came to check if you are working hard.

128
00:13:57,570 --> 00:14:00,200
Do you have any song you want to hear?

129
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:03,900
Any song is fine.

130
00:14:04,090 --> 00:14:05,030
I’ll let you choose.

131
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:08,600
Please pick a song.

132
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:10,800
Please.

133
00:14:13,110 --> 00:14:14,800
I want to sing the song for you.

134
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:25,440
The song that you sang
at my condo that night.

135
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:28,780
The song that you wrote.

136
00:14:32,050 --> 00:14:33,050
Sure.

137
00:14:40,230 --> 00:14:41,300
We’ll play ‘Your One’.

138
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:44,800
Hello.

139
00:14:46,090 --> 00:14:47,200
Tonight,

140
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:49,950
we will start off with a special song.

141
00:14:50,850 --> 00:14:52,300
It’s my self-composed song.

142
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:56,200
I wrote this song for someone,

143
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,500
someone important to me.

144
00:15:12,350 --> 00:15:16,530
♪ If love is just a game
between you and me ♪

145
00:15:17,630 --> 00:15:21,580
♪ I’ll make sure
I’m the one with the victory ♪

146
00:15:22,490 --> 00:15:26,500
♪ I want everything my way,
make you agree ♪

147
00:15:26,750 --> 00:15:30,760
♪ Your heart must belong to me ♪

148
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:34,000
♪ Just hold my gaze a little longer ♪

149
00:15:34,210 --> 00:15:36,700
♪ Move your heart a little closer ♪

150
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:41,200
♪ Let’s take the meaning of love
a little further ♪

151
00:15:41,710 --> 00:15:44,900
♪ What we have doesn't end tonight ♪

152
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:46,840
♪ I’ll love you every day ♪

153
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:51,530
♪ Close to me, your only one ♪

154
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:54,710
♪ I’ll make you love me,
make you remember ♪

155
00:15:54,750 --> 00:15:57,700
♪ I’ll keep repeating till you surrender ♪

156
00:15:58,140 --> 00:16:01,700
♪ With every touch, remember only me ♪

157
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:05,160
♪ I’ll hold you close in everything I do ♪

158
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:08,260
♪ Make it sink in, make you remember too ♪

159
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:10,780
♪ Slowly let your feelings run free ♪

160
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:14,760
♪ You’ll remember no one else but me ♪

161
00:16:15,190 --> 00:16:20,200
♪ Ohh Ohh ♪

162
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:30,870
♪ Ohh Ohh ♪

163
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:36,000
♪ Your only one ♪

164
00:16:37,150 --> 00:16:38,500
Can I have a drink with you?

165
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:45,400
Yes.

166
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:12,829
What do you want?

167
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:15,329
Did you receive the flower from me?

168
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:19,900
I told my secretary

169
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:22,599
not to accept anything from you again.

170
00:17:23,290 --> 00:17:24,200
It’s okay.

171
00:17:25,349 --> 00:17:27,400
I can go and give it to you
myself next time.

172
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:29,290
I won’t ask anyone to do that for me.

173
00:17:32,630 --> 00:17:35,980
You are still as self-centered as ever.

174
00:17:44,750 --> 00:17:46,100
Back then,

175
00:17:47,430 --> 00:17:49,500
we often listened to music together.

176
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:52,100
Do you remember it?

177
00:17:53,710 --> 00:17:57,010
We had wine while listening to music.

178
00:17:57,040 --> 00:17:58,300
It’s just the past.

179
00:17:59,150 --> 00:18:00,900
Can you stop talking about the old days?

180
00:18:01,510 --> 00:18:02,640
It won’t work on me.

181
00:18:09,570 --> 00:18:11,100
That girl, Key.

182
00:18:12,510 --> 00:18:14,000
Are you just sleeping with her?

183
00:18:15,370 --> 00:18:17,300
Or are you thinking of
getting serious with her?

184
00:18:30,570 --> 00:18:32,560
You told me

185
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:35,300
you didn’t like dating someone younger.

186
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:41,300
You liked dating someone
of the same age like me.

187
00:18:46,330 --> 00:18:50,700
It looks like Chan is uncomfortable
with you touching her.

188
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:53,800
Key.

189
00:19:02,450 --> 00:19:04,000
I thought you would avoid me.

190
00:19:05,130 --> 00:19:07,800
I saw you walk down the stage and disappear.

191
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:09,700
I just went to get changed.

192
00:19:12,730 --> 00:19:14,200
Sorry, Chan.

193
00:19:14,890 --> 00:19:21,500
I changed out of the dress you bought me
for something else.

194
00:19:23,540 --> 00:19:25,600
I guess you need to put effort into
your outfits.

195
00:19:26,410 --> 00:19:28,400
Or Chan will get bored with you.

196
00:19:31,510 --> 00:19:33,400
She never seems to get bored of me.

197
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:36,700
Right?

198
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:46,320
I don’t think we’ve officially
introduced ourselves.

199
00:19:49,090 --> 00:19:49,810
I’m Jay.

200
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,250
Chan’s ex-girlfriend.

201
00:19:55,750 --> 00:19:56,960
Nice to meet you.

202
00:20:03,550 --> 00:20:04,600
I’m Key.

203
00:20:13,110 --> 00:20:14,700
You can sleep around

204
00:20:15,930 --> 00:20:17,990
or date someone to kill time.

205
00:20:21,850 --> 00:20:22,830
I don’t mind it.

206
00:20:23,810 --> 00:20:24,800
I understand.

207
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:32,900
Please take good care of my Chan, Key.

208
00:20:35,090 --> 00:20:38,200
Don’t worry, Jay.

209
00:20:48,630 --> 00:20:49,600
Good night.

210
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:05,200
Go get your stuff.

211
00:21:05,350 --> 00:21:06,650
I’ll give you a ride back to your condo.

212
00:21:06,690 --> 00:21:08,800
Don’t you want me
to stay with you tonight?

213
00:21:13,380 --> 00:21:14,700
I have something to think about.

214
00:21:21,620 --> 00:21:22,800
About Jay,

215
00:21:24,250 --> 00:21:25,180
right?

216
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:32,800
You don’t need to pay attention to it.

217
00:21:37,550 --> 00:21:38,900
It’s about you.

218
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:41,500
How can I not pay attention to it?

219
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:48,000
Pay attention to things involving you,

220
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:51,800
it’s my job.

221
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:59,800
Whoever makes you feel bad

222
00:22:01,250 --> 00:22:02,600
or uncomfortable,

223
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:08,700
I will take care of them myself.

224
00:22:12,930 --> 00:22:14,300
Can you really do that?

225
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:16,050
Of course.

226
00:22:18,740 --> 00:22:20,200
I won’t let anyone

227
00:22:21,190 --> 00:22:25,300
hurt you or make you sad.

228
00:22:28,030 --> 00:22:29,220
I promise.

229
00:22:33,940 --> 00:22:36,300
I will be your safe zone.

230
00:22:52,420 --> 00:22:54,160
So you can also be a good girl.

231
00:22:57,150 --> 00:22:58,780
You usually act like a stubborn girl.

232
00:23:01,610 --> 00:23:03,200
I can be stubborn sometimes.

233
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:06,880
So you will want to pinch my soft cheeks.

234
00:23:08,710 --> 00:23:09,500
Then…

235
00:23:10,490 --> 00:23:13,000
Can I pinch your soft cheeks now?

236
00:23:14,430 --> 00:23:15,210
Here.

237
00:23:16,450 --> 00:23:18,320
You pinch it so often
that it’s almost bruised.

238
00:23:19,140 --> 00:23:21,400
Because you always make me
want to pinch you.

239
00:23:23,320 --> 00:23:25,100
I’ve done a lot for you.

240
00:23:26,030 --> 00:23:28,400
But you still don’t want me
to sleep over at your place.

241
00:23:29,170 --> 00:23:30,400
I’m sulking with you now.

242
00:23:31,610 --> 00:23:32,700
Stop sulking.

243
00:23:33,180 --> 00:23:34,100
Get it?

244
00:23:36,380 --> 00:23:37,610
This is cheating.

245
00:23:40,020 --> 00:23:41,100
That’s too bad.

246
00:23:42,010 --> 00:23:43,900
You agreed to be my sugar baby.

247
00:23:44,490 --> 00:23:47,500
So I’m the rule enforcer.

248
00:23:52,610 --> 00:23:55,560
Fine, the rule enforcer.

249
00:23:58,990 --> 00:24:00,400
So…

250
00:24:02,240 --> 00:24:04,000
Can I spend the night with you?

251
00:24:32,470 --> 00:24:34,000
Am I bothering you?

252
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:35,870
If I say you’re bothering me,

253
00:24:36,500 --> 00:24:37,570
will you leave?

254
00:24:40,820 --> 00:24:42,900
You can spend time comfortably at home.

255
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:45,300
I don’t get why
you want to follow me here.

256
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:48,000
I came here to take care of you

257
00:24:49,300 --> 00:24:50,920
as your…

258
00:24:50,960 --> 00:24:52,000
That’s enough.

259
00:24:53,230 --> 00:24:54,500
You can do whatever you want.

260
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:03,500
Are you sure?

261
00:25:04,620 --> 00:25:06,290
I can do whatever I want.

262
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:18,900
To be honest,

263
00:25:19,510 --> 00:25:22,400
it’s quite exciting to do it here.

264
00:25:23,470 --> 00:25:24,600
What are you doing?

265
00:25:27,620 --> 00:25:29,100
I’m doing whatever I want.

266
00:25:31,070 --> 00:25:32,200
You told me so.

267
00:25:39,900 --> 00:25:41,200
This is my office.

268
00:25:42,650 --> 00:25:44,380
Why don’t you rest your eyes a bit?

269
00:26:07,920 --> 00:26:09,040
Is it your ex?

270
00:26:20,300 --> 00:26:21,100
What’s up?

271
00:26:23,600 --> 00:26:24,850
What do you call me for?

272
00:26:51,540 --> 00:26:52,780
What are you doing here?

273
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:54,770
Where is Chan?

274
00:26:56,750 --> 00:27:00,400
I heard that
you asked the hotel owner to serve you.

275
00:27:01,880 --> 00:27:04,560
I suddenly feel eager to help her.

276
00:27:05,980 --> 00:27:06,900
Here.

277
00:27:07,570 --> 00:27:09,000
The mineral water that you ordered.

278
00:27:09,830 --> 00:27:11,760
Chan also asked me to tell you

279
00:27:12,300 --> 00:27:14,800
that she told her staff to arrange
the water for you every morning.

280
00:27:16,370 --> 00:27:17,300
Is that so?

281
00:27:18,320 --> 00:27:18,970
Okay.

282
00:27:22,450 --> 00:27:23,600
Why don’t you take it?

283
00:27:23,940 --> 00:27:25,180
Aren’t you thirsty?

284
00:27:29,580 --> 00:27:30,800
Since you are here,

285
00:27:30,950 --> 00:27:32,700
can you put it where I will use it?

286
00:27:33,550 --> 00:27:34,500
Sure.

287
00:27:35,470 --> 00:27:36,900
No problem.

288
00:27:53,830 --> 00:27:54,800
Put it here.

289
00:27:57,310 --> 00:27:58,400
Why?

290
00:27:58,630 --> 00:27:59,810
I’ll use it to rinse my mouth.

291
00:28:01,630 --> 00:28:03,080
Are you trying to get on my nerves?

292
00:28:03,810 --> 00:28:04,700
What?

293
00:28:05,160 --> 00:28:06,400
No, I’m not.

294
00:28:06,990 --> 00:28:10,480
I rinse your mouth with mineral water
to hydrate it.

295
00:28:11,120 --> 00:28:12,500
So my mouth won’t feel dry.

296
00:28:13,130 --> 00:28:15,100
Has Chan never told you this?

297
00:28:16,990 --> 00:28:18,900
She is the one who taught me this.

298
00:28:20,870 --> 00:28:21,700
No.

299
00:28:22,630 --> 00:28:24,250
I won’t follow the instruction either.

300
00:28:25,310 --> 00:28:27,560
She set the no-kiss rule with you, right?

301
00:28:31,860 --> 00:28:33,200
It means…

302
00:28:34,010 --> 00:28:35,600
you and Chan

303
00:28:36,520 --> 00:28:38,900
are not at the stage
where I have to be worried.

304
00:29:25,630 --> 00:29:27,580
Do you think you can be her girlfriend?

305
00:29:33,700 --> 00:29:36,350
All you can be is her sugar baby.

306
00:29:38,960 --> 00:29:39,800
Yes.

307
00:29:42,930 --> 00:29:44,230
I’m just her sugar baby.

308
00:29:46,780 --> 00:29:48,570
I have never been her girlfriend like you.

309
00:29:56,170 --> 00:29:57,800
But a sugar baby like me,

310
00:30:01,340 --> 00:30:03,200
I’ve never hurt her.

311
00:30:29,430 --> 00:30:30,200
Hey.

312
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:33,600
Can you stop sulking?

313
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:35,000
I don’t like it.

314
00:30:37,840 --> 00:30:39,500
What do I need to do?

315
00:30:40,340 --> 00:30:41,440
So you will like me.

316
00:30:44,860 --> 00:30:45,900
You’re doing this again.

317
00:30:46,910 --> 00:30:48,200
You’re acting like a child.

318
00:30:50,280 --> 00:30:51,480
I’m just a child.

319
00:30:55,950 --> 00:30:57,870
If you’re going to act
unreasonably like this,

320
00:30:59,370 --> 00:31:01,400
you should go back to sleep
at your condo tonight.

321
00:31:07,270 --> 00:31:10,420
You can scold me or act coldly towards me.

322
00:31:10,460 --> 00:31:11,600
I’m okay with it.

323
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:14,700
But don’t chase me away
like I were an animal.

324
00:31:15,730 --> 00:31:16,760
I’m also a human.

325
00:31:18,940 --> 00:31:20,100
So this is my fault?

326
00:31:34,850 --> 00:31:35,800
Okay.

327
00:31:37,570 --> 00:31:39,100
It’s my fault.

328
00:31:40,350 --> 00:31:41,700
I shouldn’t have done that.

329
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:46,780
I’ll sleep at my condo tonight.

330
00:31:48,310 --> 00:31:49,800
Please take care of Simba.

331
00:32:13,110 --> 00:32:14,720
We ran into each other quite often today.

332
00:32:18,190 --> 00:32:19,800
I hope that we will become closer.

333
00:32:29,340 --> 00:32:32,040
Are you two fighting because of me?

334
00:32:34,840 --> 00:32:36,100
I think you know the answer.

335
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:40,500
I can’t help it.

336
00:32:41,460 --> 00:32:42,700
This is how I am.

337
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:45,120
Why did you come back, Jay?

338
00:32:47,410 --> 00:32:48,600
I came back to you.

339
00:32:53,130 --> 00:32:54,700
I want us to get back together.

340
00:32:58,970 --> 00:33:00,500
You suddenly left me.

341
00:33:01,350 --> 00:33:02,550
Now you came back.

342
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:05,330
You expect me to simply forget
what you did to me?

343
00:33:07,320 --> 00:33:08,600
What are you thinking?

344
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:12,200
Why are you so sure
that you can do anything to me?

345
00:33:20,620 --> 00:33:21,700
Because I know

346
00:33:23,140 --> 00:33:24,470
that you still love me.

347
00:33:26,190 --> 00:33:27,900
You are just trying to deny it.

348
00:33:31,630 --> 00:33:32,370
Yeah.

349
00:33:33,440 --> 00:33:34,270
Fine.

350
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:36,870
I admit it.

351
00:33:39,230 --> 00:33:40,700
I still love you, Jay.

352
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:44,380
So?

353
00:33:52,780 --> 00:33:54,170
Let’s get back together.

354
00:34:07,690 --> 00:34:09,670
I don’t want to get hurt by you again.

355
00:34:16,460 --> 00:34:17,659
Please let me go.

356
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:20,449
I’m begging you.

357
00:35:09,820 --> 00:35:10,970
Why are you drinking like this?

358
00:35:11,920 --> 00:35:13,000
You are wasting it.

359
00:35:26,340 --> 00:35:27,500
Wasting it?

360
00:35:30,160 --> 00:35:31,330
I didn’t spill it.

361
00:35:34,240 --> 00:35:35,500
Can I tell you the truth?

362
00:35:37,660 --> 00:35:39,600
I really hit it off with you.

363
00:35:40,340 --> 00:35:41,250
You know that?

364
00:35:51,100 --> 00:35:52,100
Me too.

365
00:35:55,950 --> 00:35:57,700
I did some digging about you.

366
00:35:58,600 --> 00:35:59,740
At first,

367
00:36:00,410 --> 00:36:02,900
I thought you were clinging
to Chan for money.

368
00:36:06,130 --> 00:36:08,080
But you come from a well-known family.

369
00:36:13,120 --> 00:36:15,270
Why did you agree to be her sugar baby?

370
00:36:20,650 --> 00:36:21,700
If I tell you,

371
00:36:24,410 --> 00:36:26,120
will you get out of Chan’s life?

372
00:36:27,790 --> 00:36:29,320
Do you think I would do that?

373
00:36:34,340 --> 00:36:35,450
I know you wouldn’t.

374
00:36:38,380 --> 00:36:39,670
But I still want to ask you.

375
00:36:41,260 --> 00:36:42,360
Maybe I’ll get lucky.

376
00:36:44,750 --> 00:36:46,250
Do you like Chan that much?

377
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:57,900
I love her.

378
00:36:59,600 --> 00:37:01,300
You two have known each other
for a short time.

379
00:37:02,580 --> 00:37:03,900
Don’t you think it’s too fast

380
00:37:04,600 --> 00:37:06,160
to say you love her?

381
00:37:14,790 --> 00:37:15,740
No.

382
00:37:19,510 --> 00:37:21,100
I’ve loved her for a long time.

383
00:37:24,960 --> 00:37:26,800
Have you known her for a long time?

384
00:37:35,650 --> 00:37:37,600
It happened

385
00:37:41,710 --> 00:37:43,600
when my mom tried to abandon me.

386
00:37:49,340 --> 00:37:50,920
My mom never loved me.

387
00:39:10,780 --> 00:39:12,700
Why don’t you answer my call?

388
00:39:17,740 --> 00:39:19,500
I’m scared.

389
00:39:31,820 --> 00:39:33,760
Why are you not answering my call?

390
00:39:40,530 --> 00:39:42,800
Mom, I’m scared.

391
00:39:44,070 --> 00:39:45,150
Mom.

392
00:40:19,700 --> 00:40:21,640
Mom.

393
00:40:24,890 --> 00:40:25,700
Mom.

394
00:40:26,180 --> 00:40:28,300
Mom, where are you?

395
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:40,430
I’m scared.

396
00:40:40,470 --> 00:40:42,700
I’m really scared.

397
00:40:43,590 --> 00:40:45,100
I’m scared.

398
00:40:48,550 --> 00:40:50,800
I’m really scared.

399
00:40:52,900 --> 00:40:54,220
Mom.

400
00:41:21,810 --> 00:41:22,570
Mom.

401
00:41:31,980 --> 00:41:33,300
Mom.

402
00:42:13,110 --> 00:42:13,900
Hey.

403
00:42:16,530 --> 00:42:17,800
Are you alright?

404
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:36,500
I’m lost.

405
00:42:37,860 --> 00:42:39,200
You’re lost?

406
00:42:41,780 --> 00:42:45,900
What are you doing here alone?

407
00:42:53,110 --> 00:42:54,500
I came to watch the stars.

408
00:42:56,500 --> 00:42:57,900
Where are you going?

409
00:42:58,830 --> 00:43:00,100
Do you want me to give you a ride?

410
00:43:01,120 --> 00:43:02,880
It’s very dark here.

411
00:43:03,670 --> 00:43:05,560
It’s dangerous to walk alone.

412
00:43:07,890 --> 00:43:09,580
I want to go home.

413
00:43:10,200 --> 00:43:11,400
Do you need a ride?

414
00:43:11,790 --> 00:43:12,800
Where is your house?

415
00:43:13,480 --> 00:43:15,000
In Bangkok.

416
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:17,000
Bangkok?

417
00:43:25,050 --> 00:43:27,650
Do you want to ride with me?

418
00:43:27,980 --> 00:43:30,300
I’m also heading back to Bangkok.

419
00:43:35,970 --> 00:43:36,700
Come on.

420
00:43:37,140 --> 00:43:38,280
I’ll give you a ride.

421
00:44:34,780 --> 00:44:36,400
Did you see the picture I sent you?

422
00:44:37,230 --> 00:44:38,060
(Yes.)

423
00:44:38,100 --> 00:44:40,500
(The stars in Thailand are
much prettier than in the US.)

424
00:44:40,700 --> 00:44:42,130
If it weren’t me,

425
00:44:42,590 --> 00:44:45,900
who would take a long drive
to shoot a picture of stars for you?

426
00:44:46,670 --> 00:44:50,160
(I know that
you will do everything I ask you.)

427
00:44:50,520 --> 00:44:51,600
(Thank you.)

428
00:44:53,570 --> 00:44:54,700
You are spoiled.

429
00:44:56,350 --> 00:44:58,780
(I have to hang up. I’ve got to go.)

430
00:44:59,210 --> 00:45:00,500
(Please hurry back.)

431
00:45:00,570 --> 00:45:01,200
Alright.

432
00:45:01,240 --> 00:45:02,380
(I miss you.)

433
00:45:02,430 --> 00:45:04,400
When I’m done with my business,
I’ll hurry back.

434
00:45:04,780 --> 00:45:05,530
(Love you.)

435
00:45:06,370 --> 00:45:07,300
Love you too.

436
00:45:17,230 --> 00:45:19,130
Do you want to use my phone
to call your family?

437
00:45:25,700 --> 00:45:26,900
It’s okay.

438
00:45:33,370 --> 00:45:36,300
Can you tell me why you are here alone?

439
00:45:45,800 --> 00:45:46,900
What’s your name?

440
00:45:53,610 --> 00:45:54,800
Key.

441
00:45:56,910 --> 00:45:58,100
I’m Chan.

442
00:45:59,760 --> 00:46:04,500
Chan as in the moon?

443
00:46:05,130 --> 00:46:08,700
Yes, Chan as in the moon.

444
00:46:11,840 --> 00:46:16,100
(If we can see the stars clearly
like tonight,)

445
00:46:18,580 --> 00:46:21,900
it means we won’t see the moon.

446
00:46:25,230 --> 00:46:26,850
On the night

447
00:46:28,390 --> 00:46:30,540
when we can clearly see the moon,

448
00:46:32,720 --> 00:46:34,720
we won’t see the stars.

449
00:46:47,030 --> 00:46:50,640
Your name suits you well.

450
00:46:59,840 --> 00:47:02,200
I don’t know what you’ve been through.

451
00:47:03,680 --> 00:47:05,100
But you will get through it.

452
00:47:07,570 --> 00:47:08,700
Stay strong.

453
00:47:12,920 --> 00:47:14,200
Thank you.

454
00:47:15,990 --> 00:47:17,200
Chan.

455
00:47:55,490 --> 00:47:57,000
Thank you for giving me a ride.

456
00:47:57,870 --> 00:47:58,700
It’s not a big deal.

457
00:47:58,870 --> 00:48:00,480
You should go in. It’s late.

458
00:48:01,740 --> 00:48:02,500
Yes.

459
00:48:10,620 --> 00:48:11,360
Chan.

460
00:48:12,950 --> 00:48:13,700
Yes.

461
00:48:14,880 --> 00:48:15,800
What?

462
00:48:18,050 --> 00:48:19,500
When I’m older,

463
00:48:21,470 --> 00:48:23,200
I’ll get a moon tattoo…

464
00:48:26,640 --> 00:48:28,000
here.

465
00:48:32,230 --> 00:48:33,750
Maybe one day,

466
00:48:35,740 --> 00:48:37,550
our paths may cross again.

467
00:48:39,050 --> 00:48:40,700
This will help you remember me.

468
00:48:44,760 --> 00:48:46,000
I won’t forget you.

469
00:48:46,970 --> 00:48:47,970
You should go inside.

470
00:48:51,300 --> 00:48:52,100
Yes.

471
00:48:53,320 --> 00:48:54,670
Drive safely.

472
00:48:55,470 --> 00:48:56,300
Bye.

473
00:49:20,270 --> 00:49:21,730
You know what?

474
00:49:25,730 --> 00:49:27,200
Life…

475
00:49:28,990 --> 00:49:30,700
Life can be so cruel sometimes.

476
00:49:37,220 --> 00:49:38,900
Chan doesn’t remember me.

477
00:49:42,770 --> 00:49:44,300
She’s never remembered me.

478
00:49:47,990 --> 00:49:49,800
You are the only one she remembers.

479
00:49:53,280 --> 00:49:54,500
She loves only you.

480
00:50:00,800 --> 00:50:02,600
That’s why I can only be her sugar baby.

481
00:50:15,330 --> 00:50:16,750
Are you going to give up?

482
00:50:22,670 --> 00:50:23,500
No.

483
00:50:27,370 --> 00:50:28,780
You don’t give up.

484
00:50:31,190 --> 00:50:32,380
Neither will I.

485
00:50:36,020 --> 00:50:36,850
Good.

486
00:50:38,060 --> 00:50:39,300
That’s the spirit.

487
00:50:41,040 --> 00:50:43,180
Now, you’re worthy of being my rival.

488
00:51:08,800 --> 00:51:10,560
Are you going out to eat?
Can I come with you?

489
00:51:10,600 --> 00:51:12,520
I don’t remember inviting you.

490
00:51:12,560 --> 00:51:15,400
Do you feel intimidated by me?

491
00:51:15,910 --> 00:51:18,310
I know that I hurt you when I left you.

492
00:51:18,350 --> 00:51:19,640
But I also had no choice.

493
00:51:20,110 --> 00:51:21,240
Don’t be sad, Chan.

494
00:51:21,280 --> 00:51:22,570
I’m always your girl.

495
00:51:22,750 --> 00:51:25,630
I want to be with you
and take care of you like this.

496
00:51:25,730 --> 00:51:27,170
Between us is a business deal.

497
00:51:27,210 --> 00:51:30,780
As long as the deal is still on,
you can still do your job.

498
00:51:30,820 --> 00:51:35,100
If I fall in love with you for real,
what will you do?
